      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1331",
      "html": "<p>Hypostomus taphorni (Lilyestrom, 1984). Synonym: Cochliodon taphorni. Maximum size 228 mm SL (9 inches).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1331",
      "html": "<p>South America: Essequibo River basin, Guyana. Type locality: Río Botanamo, Río Cuyuni drainage, near the bridge on the road to Bochinche, Bolívar State, Venezuela.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1331",
      "html": "<p>Being a member of the Hypostomus cochliodon group, it will eat wood.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1331",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1331",
      "html": "<p>Previously placed in Cochliodon and now included in the larger genus Hypostomus as a member of the Hypostomus Cochliodon group. All these species have higher backs than other conspecifics and spoon-shaped teeth (like Panaque). Fishbase and CLOFFSCA disagree on size: 185 mm SL is listed in CLOFFSCA.</p>"
    },
